  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Completion Review, Rehabilitation of Freetown Water Supply Systems Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASI, with the primary responsibility of undertaking the Project Completion Review of the Rehabilitation of Freetown&apos;s Water Supply System Programme in Sierra Leone, had the key objective of collating evidence from research and interviews into a final completion report. ASI delivered 2 milestones: (i) a draft PCR, narrative, and short lessons learnt report, and (ii) a final PCR, narrative, and short lessons learnt.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project completed a Project Completion Review (PCR) of the Rehabilitation of Freetown&#x2019;s Water Supply System Programme in Sierra Leone. The Freetown Water Supply Rehabilitation project commenced in June 2016 and was designed to address water insecurity across Freetown by providing safe, and accessible water supply year-round for 600,000 residents across the city and providing new conections for at least 90,000 people. Our PCR assesses the programme&#x2019;s performance across its lifetime and provides a final assessment against its logframe.</narrative>
  </description>
